{"kind":"event","event_id":3417,"event_uid":"01M2JY69N5CM7WB2KXMKPWW8SD","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":169,"issue_uid":"01M2JY2GNCSDAEGBFH1RT9MKED","issue_short_id":"mked","actor":"exam:1@run-142","hlc_physical_ms":1789489522341,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2d6aea0724ba8c98fe8df5baedf15c1c930ed1edea39bc1f81a07719744519e9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2JY69N40ADJ5AFRV32VDV5A","author":"exam:1@run-142","body":"examiner (run-142 task 1): writing the exam at tests/exams/run_142/test_release_0_3_29.py (EXAM PATHS maps it there from the Proof's tests/test_release_0_3_29.py; nothing is left at the Proof path).\n\nReading of the legs I am encoding:\n- [M1/leg a] four assertions: plugin.json's top-level version == the string '0.3.29'; marketplace.json's plugins[name=ultrapowers].version == '0.3.29'; and, reading each file at $ULTRA_BASE via 'git show', the base object with only that one version key rewritten to 0.3.29 must equal the working-tree object — i.e. no other key changed. That is the first Run: line as pytest.\n- [M2/leg b] the Versioning bullet is the text sed -n '/\\*\\*Versioning:\\*\\*/,/^- \\*\\*/p' returns (start line inclusive, terminating '- **' line inclusive, newlines folded to spaces) — I replicate those sed range semantics in Python rather than shelling out. Asserted: the ordered regex 0\\.3\\.29.*today.*a release is a fleet plan.*merged by the.*gh release create matches (second Run:), each of those five needles is present on its own so a failure names which one is missing, and re.findall('0\\.3\\.28[^0-9]*today') is empty (third Run:).\n- [M3/leg c] the two manifests' version strings are equal (fourth Run:), and that one shared string is '0.3.29' (M3's 'one and the same' read together with M1's exact value, so the leg is not green against a stub that leaves both at 0.3.28); and 'git diff --name-only $ULTRA_BASE' names no path outside .claude-plugin/plugin.json, .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, CLAUDE.md, tests/exams/ and tests/test_release_0_3_29.py (fifth Run:).\n\nBase sha comes from $ULTRA_BASE (CONTRACT: every exam command runs with it set), falling back to this run's BASE fdb2dd27 when a human runs the file by hand. The last Run: (wc -w over skills/*/SKILL.md and fleet/roles/*.md) is a report that gates nothing per CLAUDE.md §Judgment prompts, so it is not a leg and earns no assertion.\n\nExpected red at BASE: both manifests read 0.3.28, so the M1 and M3 exact-value assertions fail; CLAUDE.md's bullet still says 0.3.28 today, so M2 fails. No import, fixture or path failure.","created_at":"2026-09-15T16:25:22.340460776Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T16:25:22.341Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":3418,"event_uid":"01M2JY8B78Q4HKZRC4D2VV4RVE","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":169,"issue_uid":"01M2JY2GNCSDAEGBFH1RT9MKED","issue_short_id":"mked","actor":"exam:1@run-142","hlc_physical_ms":1789489589480,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"3dd369f8d9512e48039d539f6dff799135553e1291d0ae893c001ff463262f7a","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2JY8B763ZNTYT8X6J33R97A","author":"exam:1@run-142","body":"examiner: exam handed in at tests/exams/run_142/test_release_0_3_29.py — 13 tests, all three legs covered, nothing under unsatisfiable, nothing left at the Proof path tests/test_release_0_3_29.py.\n\nVerified at BASE fdb2dd27 with ULTRA_BASE set: 8 failed, 5 passed. The 8 failures are exactly the absent bump — both manifests still read 0.3.28 (M1 x4, M3 x1), and CLAUDE.md's bullet still reads 0.3.29-absent / 0.3.28 today (M2 x3). No import, collection or fixture error. The 5 that already pass are the M2 phrases M2 pins as unchanged ('today', 'a release is a fleet plan', 'merged by the', 'gh release create') and the M3 diff check, which is green on a clean tree by construction and goes red only if the implementer touches a fourth file.\n\nThen applied the intended edit (both manifests 0.3.28 -> 0.3.29, and the single '0.3.28' -> '0.3.29' in the bullet's 'plugin.json carries ... today' clause) and re-ran: 13 passed. Reverted; the tree is clean but for the exam. Worth recording for the implementer: the CLAUDE.md sentence at line 187, '0.3.28 stabilizes the 0.3 feature set and is not 0.4.0', sits in the Working-with-the-operator section, outside the sed range the M2 leg reads, so leaving that history in place (as the Context says to) keeps the exam green.\n\nNote for a later reader on one judgment call: test_m3_both_manifests_carry_one_and_the_same_version asserts both a == b (the fourth Run: verbatim) and that the shared string is '0.3.29'. The equality alone is true at BASE, where both read 0.3.28, so on its own that leg would pass against a stub; M3's 'one and the same version string' read together with M1's 'is the string 0.3.29' fixes what that one string must be, and the second assert is what keeps the leg live.","created_at":"2026-09-15T16:26:29.478812958Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T16:26:29.48Z"}
